<report>
<line><title>Directly Standardized Rates</title></line>
<line></line>
<line>Rates are expressed per <in>units</in> of person time:</line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th>Index events</th><th>Index PT</th><th>Index rate</th><th>Reference size</th><th>Weight</th></tr>
<block name="inputs"><tr><td><in>idxy</in></td><td><in>idxn</in></td><td><in>idxr</in></td><td><in>refn</in></td><td><in>refw</in></td></tr></block>
</table>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th>Index rate</th><th><ci>Exact <in>pc</in>% confidence interval</ci></th><th></th></tr>
<block name="cis"><tr><td><in>idxr</in></td><td><ci><in>from</in>  to  <in>to</in></ci></td><td><in>label</in></td></tr></block>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>Total events = <in>events</in></line>
<line>Adjusted events = <in>stde</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Crude rate = <in>crude</in></line>
<line>Adjusted rate R = <in>stdr</in></line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Any rates (binomial model)</u></line>
<line>Approximate standard error of R = <in>ser_any</in></line>
<line><ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>from_any</in> to <in>to_any</in></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>Small rates (Poisson model)</line>
<line>Approximate standard error of R = <in>ser_small</in></line>
<line><ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>from_small</in> to <in>to_small</in></ci></line>
<line><ci>Improved approximate (Dobson) <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>from_dobson</in> to <in>to_dobson</in></ci></line>
</report>
